    <li>Check whether <span set:html={rich('[[6]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[8]]')} />, and <span set:html={rich('[[11]]')} /> form a triple. Answer: no. <span set:html={rich('[[6^2+8^2=36+64=100]]')} />, but <span set:html={rich('[[11^2=121]]')} />, so the two sides differ.</li>
    <li>Identify whether <span set:html={rich('[[9]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[12]]')} />, and <span set:html={rich('[[15]]')} /> are primitive. Answer: non-primitive. The numbers share the factor <span set:html={rich('[[3]]')} />, and dividing by <span set:html={rich('[[3]]')} /> gives the primitive triple <span set:html={rich('[[(3, 4, 5)]]')} />.</li>
