    <li>Generate a triple using <span set:html={rich('[[m=4]]')} /> and <span set:html={rich('[[n=1]]')} />. Answer: <span set:html={rich('[[(8, 15, 17)]]')} />. <span set:html={rich('[[a=16-1=15]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[b=8]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[c=16+1=17]]')} />, with the legs sorted ascending.</li>
    <li>Identify whether <span set:html={rich('[[m=3]]')} /> and <span set:html={rich('[[n=1]]')} /> produce a primitive triple. Answer: no. The parameters are coprime but both odd, so the result is the non-primitive triple <span set:html={rich('[[(6, 8, 10)]]')} />.</li>
    <li>Find the common multiplier between <span set:html={rich('[[3]]')} />-<span set:html={rich('[[4]]')} />-<span set:html={rich('[[5]]')} /> and <span set:html={rich('[[15]]')} />-<span set:html={rich('[[20]]')} />-<span set:html={rich('[[25]]')} />. Answer: <span set:html={rich('[[5]]')} />. Each side of <span set:html={rich('[[(3, 4, 5)]]')} /> multiplied by <span set:html={rich('[[5]]')} /> gives <span set:html={rich('[[(15, 20, 25)]]')} />.</li>
